 "instructions": "Memory between sessions lives in these tools, not in files.\nSearch when the user refers to shared context you lack or a stored preference could settle an ambiguity; otherwise do not.\nWrite unasked whenever something durable appears: a preference, a decision, a tool or config fact, finished work and its reason.\nA staleness_verdict other than fresh means a check failed or a record objects; `reason` names it and its remedy. Act on it before relying on the memory.\nSay briefly when a memory shaped your reply. In a loop, call episode(action='handoff') at each iteration's start.",
